  "goodToKnow": "Der Ankläger (die Anklägerin) is a prosecutor or accuser. In German criminal trials, the prosecution is led by the Staatsanwaltschaft, and victims can join as Nebenkläger (joint plaintiffs) with their own lawyer. At the Nuremberg Trials (1945–46), the Allied chief prosecutors were called Hauptankläger. Anklagen means to charge, and die Anklage is the indictment. The plural is the same."
